      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "High blood pressure (hypertension) is usually a \"silent killer\" with no outward signs or symptoms until it reaches a dangerous stage.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "no outward signs or symptoms"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "The Silent Nature of Hypertension"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "No early warnings: You can have high blood pressure for years without knowing it while it damages your heart, brain, and kidneys."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The only true sign: A clinical measurement using a blood pressure cuff is the only reliable way to know your numbers.",
            "snippet_links": [
              {
                "text": "blood pressure cuff",
                "link": "https://medlineplus.gov/ency/article/000468.htm"
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Normal vs. High: Normal blood pressure is below 120/80 mm Hg. Stage 1 high blood pressure starts at 130/80 mm Hg or higher."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Warning Signs of a Dangerous Spike (Hypertensive Crisis)"
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "When blood pressure spikes drastically above 180/120 mm Hg, it can cause severe symptoms that require emergency medical care. Seek emergency help by calling 911 if extreme high blood pressure is accompanied by:",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          5
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Severe, sudden headache"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Shortness of breath or difficulty breathing"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Chest pain or tightness"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Sudden vision changes or blurry vision"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Confusion, dizziness, or fatigue"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Signs of a stroke (slurred speech, facial drooping, or weakness on one side)"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          2,
          5,
          8,
          9
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Learn more about managing your risks with the American Heart Association or guidelines from the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention .",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "American Heart Association",
            "link": "https://www.heart.org/en/health-topics/high-blood-pressure"
          },
          {
            "text": "Centers for Disease Control and Prevention",
            "link": "https://www.cdc.gov/high-blood-pressure"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          3
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your most recent blood pressure reading if you have one"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you are looking for prevention tips or home monitoring advice"
          }
        ]
      },
